  "description": "Introducing the world’s biggest Quadangle bike, the 32” Colossal Quadangle, a bike that's truly a work of art. The limited-edition Cr-Mo Quadangle has been scaled up into a unprecedented size built around 32” Bozack tires and featuring a lengthy 24.7” top tube with internal cable routing. The rear end of the bike remains compact, so you can easily pop that wheel up. The lightweight TSC cranks provide a powerful feel, while the Shimano MT200 hydraulic disc brakes give you precise control. The 8.25” Colossal 4pc Cruiser bars and Scot Enterprises stem provide a comfortable feel and sturdy cockpit. To top it off, this bike comes equipped with ODI Longneck grips, a new SE Captive seat, and a Quadangle padset. No doubt about it, this bike is the new trend setter!",
